# Line endings are the repo's decision, not the contributor's machine's.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with the common `core.autocrlf=true` gets a
# CRLF working copy while the index stores LF. Prettier's `endOfLine: "lf"`
# then fails `yarn format:check` on every tracked file locally, while CI
# (Linux, LF) passes — a gate that is green where nobody looks. Forcing LF on
# checkout also keeps the Docker build context byte-identical across machines.
#
# The index already stores LF, so this changes checkout behaviour only; it
# introduces no content churn.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch.
*.woff2 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
